## hexagon integration-test Admin API policy
##
## Install in dom0 as /etc/qubes/policy.d/30-hexagon-test.policy, then replace
## every "MGMT_QUBE" below with the qube that runs the hexagon integration tests
## (the AppVM you check the repo out in). Remove the file to revoke all access.
##
## Validate before relying on it:   qubes-policy-lint /etc/qubes/policy.d/30-hexagon-test.policy
##
## Model: the management qube may CREATE test VMs and has full control over only
## the VMs tagged "hexagon-test". A freshly created VM carries the unforgeable
## "created-by-MGMT_QUBE" tag, which bootstraps applying the "hexagon-test" tag;
## from then on the tag-scoped rules below cover everything.
##
## Columns:  SERVICE  ARGUMENT  SOURCE  TARGET  ACTION [params]
## "@adminvm" is dom0; admin calls execute there, hence "target=@adminvm".

## --- Create test VMs (global scope: the VM doesn't exist yet) ---
admin.vm.Create.AppVM    *              MGMT_QUBE  @adminvm                     allow target=@adminvm

## --- Read-only introspection of all VMs (the `hexagon ls` path enumerates
##     every domain and reads its tags/features/properties) ---
## NB: admin.vm.List needs TWO rules. The call is directed at dom0, so it needs a
## rule matching @adminvm; qubesd then filters the returned list per-VM, so an
## @anyvm rule is also required for templates / other VMs to be visible at all.
admin.vm.List            *              MGMT_QUBE  @adminvm                     allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.List            *              MGMT_QUBE  @anyvm                       allow target=@adminvm
admin.label.List         *              MGMT_QUBE  @adminvm                     allow target=@adminvm
admin.pool.List          *              MGMT_QUBE  @adminvm                     allow target=@adminvm
## `hexagon ls` enumerates every visible VM (incl. dom0) and reads each one's
## tags/properties, so reads are granted on both @anyvm and @adminvm (dom0).
admin.vm.property.Get    *              MGMT_QUBE  @anyvm                       allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.property.Get    *              MGMT_QUBE  @adminvm                     allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.feature.Get     *              MGMT_QUBE  @anyvm                       allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.feature.Get     *              MGMT_QUBE  @adminvm                     allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.tag.Get         *              MGMT_QUBE  @anyvm                       allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.tag.Get         *              MGMT_QUBE  @adminvm                     allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.tag.List        *              MGMT_QUBE  @anyvm                       allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.tag.List        *              MGMT_QUBE  @adminvm                     allow target=@adminvm

## --- Bootstrap: tag VMs we just created with "hexagon-test" ---
admin.vm.tag.Set         +hexagon-test  MGMT_QUBE  @tag:created-by-MGMT_QUBE    allow target=@adminvm

## --- Manage our test VMs, scoped by the tag (explicit services; no wildcard) ---
admin.vm.Start           *              MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test            allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.Shutdown        *              MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test            allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.Kill            *              MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test            allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.Remove          *              MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test            allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.property.Set    *              MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test            allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.feature.Set     *              MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test            allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.tag.Set         *              MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test            allow target=@adminvm
admin.vm.tag.Remove      *              MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test            allow target=@adminvm

## Rebooting a netvm with attached clients: hexagon runs `sudo poweroff` *inside*
## the VM (avoids the "VM in use" error), which needs qubes.VMShell to it. This is
## a regular qrexec call into the VM (no target= redirect). Scoped to test VMs.
qubes.VMShell            *              MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test            allow

## `hexagon reboot -t` opens a terminal in the VM via qubes.StartApp (also a
## regular qrexec call). hexagon exits non-zero if it's refused, so the
## integration test doubles as a check that this grant is in place.
qubes.StartApp           +qubes-run-terminal MGMT_QUBE  @tag:hexagon-test       allow
